notes:
Mapping decisions:
- language_switch per_question: the question papers are set both in Hindi and English (notice Section II A Note (iii), PDF p.26).
- numeric_input left unset: the paper has no numeric-entry questions, and the schema requires a value (schema change requested).
- question_count left unset: the notice does not state the number of questions.
- group prelims: both papers are on the same day (notice PDF p.5); order follows the official paper numbers (Paper I, Paper II); the break is not stated.
- instructions: summary in our own words of the notice paragraphs cited in the source; Hindi translated.

Open questions:
- The Civil Services Examination, 2027 notice is not published yet (checked 2026-10-30). This is the latest official pattern; re-verify and version it as upsc-cse-2027 when UPSC notifies it.
- The UPSC Annual Calendar 2027 (https://www.upsc.gov.in/sites/default/files/Calendar-Year-2027-Engl-200526.pdf) could not be opened from this environment (HTTP 403), so the 2027 notification and Prelims dates are not recorded.
- The number of questions in each paper and the marks per question are not stated in the notice. They are printed on the question booklets, which UPSC publishes on its exam page; those pages could not be opened from this environment (HTTP 403), so question_count stays null.
- Session timings (forenoon and afternoon) are not stated in the notice; they appear on the e-Admit Card. shift_timings stays null.
- The notice says the papers are set in Hindi and English but does not say which version prevails when they differ.

